linux-thermal-control (0.5.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show only one representative CPU temperature and one representative GPU
    temperature, preferring package-level sensors over per-core duplicates.
  * Apply thermal-mode and edited custom-curve requests immediately without a
    confirmation dialog.
  * Add representative temperature-sensor selection regression tests.

 -- Linux Thermal Control Maintainers <cfys-028@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 14:30:00 +0800

linux-thermal-control (0.5.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Clevo acpi_call response parsing by truncating at the first NUL byte
    instead of deleting NUL bytes and concatenating stale kernel-buffer data.
  * Accept valid responses such as "0x69\\0alled" as 0x69 while preserving
    rejection of real ACPI error tokens.
  * Reload systemd and system D-Bus configuration before starting the daemon on
    first installation, and restart the service on fresh installs and upgrades.
  * Add ACPI response and maintainer-script regression tests.

 -- Linux Thermal Control Maintainers <cfys-028@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 10:45:00 +0800

